From: Stefano Bocconi <Stefano.Bocconi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:50:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build the plain UDP loop on every platform that is not unix

server.go calls srv.listenUDP, which only server_recvmmsg.go (unix) and
server_no_recvmmsg.go (windows) define. On any other platform the package
does not compile, js/wasm (a browser) and wasip1/wasm among them:

  ./server.go:202:7: srv.listenUDP undefined (type *Server has no field or method listenUDP)

So a program that only builds, signs and sends messages cannot be built
for WebAssembly either, although it never starts a server.

server_no_recvmmsg.go reads one message at a time through net.PacketConn
and needs nothing from Windows. Build it on every platform that is not
unix, as listen_no_socket_options.go already does for listenTCP on the
platforms without socket options.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

Notes (not part of the commit message; git am drops them):

Base: codeberg.org/miekg/dns v0.6.117, the latest release when this was
written. It also applies to v0.6.82, which has the same file. Apply in a
copy of that release with "git am" or "git apply".

Tested with Go 1.27.0 on v0.6.117: without the change, "GOOS=js
GOARCH=wasm go build ./" fails as above; with it, the package and dnshttp
build for js/wasm, wasip1/wasm, windows/amd64, linux/amd64 and
darwin/arm64, and "go vet" is clean for windows. With Go 1.26.4 on
v0.6.82: the same, and plan9/amd64 builds too. Builds for unix do not
change, as the file stays excluded there.

 server_no_recvmmsg.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server_no_recvmmsg.go b/server_no_recvmmsg.go
index 7b7b646..ae82288 100644
--- a/server_no_recvmmsg.go
+++ b/server_no_recvmmsg.go
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-//go:build windows
+//go:build !unix
 
 package dns
 
